A liquidity limit of a maximum tradable Vega of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{max}}" display="inline"><semantics id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1a"><msub id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml">𝒱</mi><mi id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml">max</mi></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1b"><apply id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.cmml" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2">𝒱</ci><ci id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3">max</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m6.1c">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> could then be implemented by
the map:</p>
