<div id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout, we assume that the non-negative adapted cost functions are normalized to
<math id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(0)=0" display="inline"><semantics id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1a"><mrow id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.cmml"><mrow id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.cmml"><msub id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.2.cmml">c</mi><mi id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.3" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.3.cmml">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.1" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.3.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.3.2.1" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.cmml">(</mo><mn id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo stretchy="false" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.3.2.2" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.1" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.3" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.3.cmml">0</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2"><eq id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.1"></eq><apply id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2"><times id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.1"></times><apply id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.2">𝑐</ci><ci id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.2.2.3">𝑘</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.1">0</cn></apply><cn type="integer" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1.2.3">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p3.1.m1.1c">c_{k}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and that they are
upper semi-continuous.<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>This property is needed in the proof of proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 4.9. ‣ 4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>.</span></span></span> In our numerical examples we have
assumed zero transaction costs at maturity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our setup includes the following effects:</p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
