<p id="S3.2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span>
</h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The methodology developed in this article can also be
applied to approximate optimal hedging strategies in a setting where
the price <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1a"><msub id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">p</mi><mn id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">0</mn></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.2">𝑝</ci><cn type="integer" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1.1.3">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.m1.1c">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is given exogenously: fix a loss function
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\colon\mathbb{R}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2a"><mrow id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.cmml"><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.2.cmml">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml">:</mo><mrow id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.cmml"><mi id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.2.cmml">ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.1.cmml">→</mo><mrow id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.2.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.1.cmml">[</mo><mn id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.1.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.2.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.1.cmml">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.2.cmml">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.2.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.1.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2b"><apply id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3"><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.1">:</ci><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.2">ℓ</ci><apply id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3"><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.1">→</ci><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.2">ℝ</ci><interval closure="closed-open" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.3.3.3.2"><cn type="integer" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.1.1">0</cn><infinity id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2.2"></infinity></interval></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.m2.2c">\ell\colon\mathbb{R}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}&gt;0" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1a"><mrow id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.2" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.2.cmml">p</mi><mn id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.3.cmml">0</mn></msub><mo id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.1" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml">&gt;</mo><mn id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.3" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml">0</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1b"><apply id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1"><gt id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.1"></gt><apply id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.2">𝑝</ci><cn type="integer" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.3">0</cn></apply><cn type="integer" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1.1.3">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.m3.1c">p_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is given, for example being the result of
trading derivatives in the market at competitive prices, without taking into
account risk-management. The agent then wishes to minimize her loss
at maturity, i.e. she defines an optimal hedging strategy as a
minimizer to</p>
