<math id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(0)\leq\rho(0)" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2a"><mrow id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.cmml"><mrow id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.cmml"><mi id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.2.cmml">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.3.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.3.2.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.cmml">(</mo><mn id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.1.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.3.2.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.1.cmml">≤</mo><mrow id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.cmml"><mi id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml">ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.3.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.3.2.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.cmml">(</mo><mn id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.2.cmml">0</mn><mo stretchy="false" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.3.2.2" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2b"><apply id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3"><leq id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.1"></leq><apply id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2"><times id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.1"></times><ci id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.2.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.2.2">𝜋</ci><cn type="integer" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.1.1">0</cn></apply><apply id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3"><times id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.1"></times><ci id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.3.3.2">𝜌</ci><cn type="integer" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.2.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2.2">0</cn></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.3.m3.2c">\pi(0)\leq\rho(0)</annotation></semantics></math> for any choice of risk measure <math id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1a"><mi id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1.1.cmml">ρ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1b"><ci id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1.1">𝜌</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.4.m4.1c">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in
(<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). Under the present assumptions the converse
inequality is also true: Since <math id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline"><semantics id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1a"><mi id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1.1" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1.1.cmml">S</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1b"><ci id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1.1.cmml" xref="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1.1">𝑆</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S3.SS2.2.p1.5.m5.1c">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale, it holds that</p>
