<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.25" class="ltx_p">is called a
(feed forward) neural network. Here the <span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">activation function</span>
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1.1.cmml">σ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1.1">𝜎</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6.m1.1c">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is applied componentwise. <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1.1.cmml">L</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1.1">𝐿</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.7.m2.1c">L</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of
