</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that the information available in our market at <math id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1a"><msub id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">t</mi><mi id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">k</mi></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.2">𝑡</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1.1.3">𝑘</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS2.p3.1.m1.1c">t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is described
by the observed maximal feature set <math id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{0},\ldots,I_{k}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3a"><mrow id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.3.cmml"><msub id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.2.cmml">I</mi><mn id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.3.cmml">0</mn></msub><mo id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.3" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.3.cmml">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml">…</mi><mo id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.4" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.3.cmml">,</mo><msub id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.2.cmml">I</mi><mi id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.3" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.3.cmml">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3b"><list id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2"><apply id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.2">𝐼</ci><cn type="integer" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.2.2.1.1.3">0</cn></apply><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.1.1">…</ci><apply id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.2">𝐼</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3.3.2.2.3">𝑘</ci></apply></list></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS2.p3.2.m2.3c">I_{0},\ldots,I_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our trading strategies should therefore depend on this information and on our previous
position in our tradable assets. This gives rise to the following semi-recurrent deep neural network structure
for our unconstrained trading strategies:</p>
