<p id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{n}\in\mathcal{H}_{M}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1a"><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.cmml"><msup id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.2.cmml">δ</mi><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.3.cmml">n</mi></msup><mo id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.1.cmml">∈</mo><msub id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml">ℋ</mi><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml">M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1"><in id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.1"></in><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.2">𝛿</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.2.3">𝑛</ci></apply><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.2">ℋ</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1.1.3.3">𝑀</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.10.m1.1c">\delta^{n}\in\mathcal{H}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1.1.cmml">M</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1.1">𝑀</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.11.m2.1c">M</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, one obtains
<math id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{M}(X)\leq\pi(X)+\varepsilon" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2a"><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.cmml"><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.cmml"><msup id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.2.cmml">π</mi><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.3.cmml">M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.3.2.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.cmml">(</mo><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.1.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.1.1.cmml">X</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.1.cmml">≤</mo><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.cmml"><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.2.cmml">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.3.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.3.2.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml">(</mo><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.2.cmml">X</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.1" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.1.cmml">+</mo><mi id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.3" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.3.cmml">ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2b"><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3"><leq id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.1"></leq><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2"><times id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.1"></times><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.2">𝜋</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.2.2.3">𝑀</ci></apply><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.1.1">𝑋</ci></apply><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3"><plus id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.1"></plus><apply id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2"><times id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.1"></times><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.2.2">𝜋</ci><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.2">𝑋</ci></apply><ci id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2.3.3.3">𝜀</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS2.7.p6.12.m3.2c">\pi^{M}(X)\leq\pi(X)+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#S4.Ex4" title="4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>), as desired.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Numerical solution for OCE-risk measures</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2 (Universal approximation, [Hor91]). ‣ 4.1. Universal approximation by neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and
Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 4.9. ‣ 4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a> give a theoretical justification for
using hedging strategies built from neural networks, we now turn to
computational considerations: how can we calculate a (close-to)
optimal parameter <math id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta_{M}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1a"><mrow id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">θ</mi><mo id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml">∈</mo><msub id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml">Θ</mi><mi id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml">M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1"><in id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.1"></in><ci id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.2">𝜃</ci><apply id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.2">Θ</ci><ci id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1.1.3.3">𝑀</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS3.p1.1.m1.1c">\theta\in\Theta_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> for (<a href="#S4.Ex4" title="4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>)?</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To explain the key ideas we focus on the case when <math id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1.1.cmml">ρ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1.1">𝜌</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS3.p2.1.m1.1c">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is an OCE
risk measure (see (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2. Optimized certainty equivalents ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>)) and no trading constraints are present, the case of general risk measures is treated below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Inserting the definition of <math id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml">ρ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1">𝜌</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS3.p3.1.m1.1c">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, see (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2. Optimized certainty equivalents ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>), into
(<a href="#S4.Ex4" title="4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), the optimization problem can be rewritten as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
