<p id="S4.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Generally, to find a local minimum of a differentiable function <math id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1.1.cmml">J</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1.1">𝐽</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS3.p3.4.m1.1c">J</annotation></semantics></math>, one may use a <span id="S4.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gradient descent</span> algorithm: Starting with an initial guess <math id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(0)}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1a"><msup id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.2" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.2.cmml">θ</mi><mrow id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.cmml">(</mo><mn id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1b"><apply id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.2.2">𝜃</ci><cn type="integer" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1.1.1.1">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS3.p3.5.m2.1c">\theta^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, one iteratively defines</p>
