<li id="S4.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ML2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\omega_{m})" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2a"><mrow id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.cmml"><mrow id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.cmml"><msub id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.cmml"><mo id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.2.cmml">∇</mo><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.3" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.3.cmml">θ</mi></msub><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.2.cmml">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.2.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">(</mo><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml">θ</mi><mo id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.3" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">,</mo><msub id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml">ω</mi><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml">m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.4" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2b"><apply id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2"><times id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.2"></times><apply id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3"><apply id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.2">∇</ci><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.1.3">𝜃</ci></apply><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.3.2">𝐽</ci></apply><interval closure="open" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1"><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.1.1">𝜃</ci><apply id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.2">𝜔</ci><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2.2.1.1.1.3">𝑚</ci></apply></interval></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1.m1.2c">\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\omega_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated
efficiently for each <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml">m</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1.1">𝑚</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.2.m2.1c">m</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. using backpropagation.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of the present section is to show that for a general class of
convex risk measures (including all coherent ones) one can approximate
(<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) by a minimax problem over neural networks and
that the objective functional of this approximate problem also has
these two key properties, making it amenable to deep learning
optimization techniques.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1a"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml">𝒫</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1.1">𝒫</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p3.1.m1.1c">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of probability measures on <math id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,\mathcal{F})" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2a"><mrow id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.2" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.2.1" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml">Ω</mi><mo id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.2.cmml">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.2.3" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml">)</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2b"><interval closure="open" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.3.2"><ci id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.1.1">Ω</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2.2">ℱ</ci></interval></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p3.2.m2.2c">(\Omega,\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math>. The
following result serves as a starting point:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.12</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robust representation of convex risk measures)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span>
</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\colon\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1a"><mrow id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml">:</mo><mrow id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.1.cmml">→</mo><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml">ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1">:</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2">𝜌</ci><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.1">→</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.2">𝒳</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.3.3">ℝ</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1.m1.1c">\rho\colon\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex risk measure. Then
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.cmml">ρ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1.1">𝜌</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.2.m2.1c">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1.3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(X)=\max_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{P}}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[-X]-\alpha(\mathbb{Q})\right),\quad X\in\mathcal{X}," display="block"><semantics id="S4.E9.m1.3a"><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1"><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.3.cmml"><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.cmml"><mi id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.2.cmml">ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.3.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.3.2.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.cmml">(</mo><mi id="S4.E9.m1.1.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.1.1.cmml">X</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.3.2.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.4.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml"><munder id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">max</mi><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.2.cmml">ℚ</mi><mo id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.3.cmml">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder><mo id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.2a" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml">⁡</mo><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.2.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml"><mo id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.2.2.2" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml">(</mo><mrow id="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2.2.2.1" xref="S4.E9.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.