<p id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1a"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1.1.cmml">ℳ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1.1">ℳ</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.2.m1.1c">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of measurable functions mapping from
<math id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r(n+1)}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1a"><mrow id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.cmml"><msup id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.2.cmml">ℝ</mi><mrow id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.3.cmml">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.2.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">(</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">n</mi><mo id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">+</mo><mn id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.1" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.1.cmml">→</mo><mi id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.3" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.3.cmml">ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1b"><apply id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2"><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.1">→</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.2.2">ℝ</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1"><times id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.2"></times><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.3">𝑟</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1"><plus id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1"></plus><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2">𝑛</ci><cn type="integer" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3">1</cn></apply></apply></apply><ci id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1.2.3">ℝ</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.2.p1.3.m2.1c">\mathbb{R}^{r(n+1)}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the second step we rely on
(<a href="#S4.E11" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.5. Extension to general risk measures ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>) to prove the statement.</p>
</div>
