<math id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1a"><mrow id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.2.cmml">n</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.1.cmml">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.3.cmml">∞</mi></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1b"><apply id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1"><ci id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.1">→</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.2">𝑛</ci><infinity id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1.1.3"></infinity></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.7.m5.1c">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this with (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.5. Extension to general risk measures ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>), one obtains
that for all <math id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1a"><mi id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1.1.cmml">n</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1.1">𝑛</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.6.p5.8.m6.1c">n</annotation></semantics></math> large enough,
