<p id="S4.SS5.p6.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1a"><msub id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.2.cmml">λ</mi><mn id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.3.cmml">0</mn></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.2">𝜆</ci><cn type="integer" id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1.1.3">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p6.3.m1.1c">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
Lagrange multiplier.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p">We conclude this section by arguing that the objective <math id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1a"><mi id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1.1.cmml">J</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1.1">𝐽</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p7.1.m1.1c">J</annotation></semantics></math> in
(<a href="#S4.E19" title="In 4.5. Extension to general risk measures ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.19</span></a>) indeed satisfies (ML1) and (ML2). This is
standard (c.f. Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3. Numerical solution for OCE-risk measures ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) for all terms in the
sum except for <math id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}(F^{\theta_{1}}\circ\bar{I})" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1a"><mrow id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.cmml"><mover accent="true" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml">α</mi><mo id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">(</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><msup id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.cmml">F</mi><msub id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.2.cmml">θ</mi><mn id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.3" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.3.cmml">1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">∘</mo><mover accent="true" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2.cmml">I</mi><mo id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1b"><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1"><times id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.2"></times><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3"><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.1">¯</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.3.2">𝛼</ci></apply><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1"><compose id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.1"></compose><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.2">𝐹</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.2">𝜃</ci><cn type="integer" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.3">1</cn></apply></apply><apply id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3"><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.1">¯</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1.1.1.1.1.3.2">𝐼</ci></apply></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p7.2.m2.1c">\bar{\alpha}(F^{\theta_{1}}\circ\bar{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and so we
only consider this term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.4" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1a"><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1.1.cmml">Ω</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1.1">Ω</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p8.1.m1.1c">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is finite and consists of <math id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1a"><mi id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1.1.cmml">N</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1b"><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1.1">𝑁</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p8.2.m2.1c">N</annotation></semantics></math> elements, thus
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\{X\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}\}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2a"><mrow id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.3" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.3.cmml">𝒳</mi><mo id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.2" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.2.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.1.cmml">{</mo><mi id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.1.1.cmml">X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.1.cmml">:</mo><mrow id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.cmml"><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml">→</mo><mi id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml">ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.4" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.1.cmml">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2b"><apply id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2"><eq id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.2"></eq><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.3">𝒳</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1"><csymbol cd="latexml" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.2">conditional-set</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.1.1">𝑋</ci><apply id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1"><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.1">→</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.2">Ω</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2.2.1.1.1.3">ℝ</ci></apply></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p8.3.m3.2c">\mathcal{X}=\{X\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math> can be identified with
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1a"><msup id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.2" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.2.cmml">ℝ</mi><mi id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.3" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.3.cmml">N</mi></msup><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1b"><apply id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.2">ℝ</ci><ci id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1.1.3">𝑁</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.SS5.p8.4.m4.1c">\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. As for standard backpropagation the compositional structure
can be used for efficient computation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.14</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span>
</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1a"><mover accent="true" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">α</mi><mo id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml">¯</mo></mover><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.1">¯</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1.1.2">𝛼</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.m1.1c">\bar{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended to
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}\colon\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1a"><mrow id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.cmml"><mover accent="true" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.2.cmml">α</mi><mo id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.1.cmml">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml">:</mo><mrow id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.2" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml">→</mo><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.3" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.3.cmml">ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1b"><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.1">:</ci><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.1">¯</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.2.2">𝛼</ci></apply><apply id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.1">→</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.2">𝒳</ci><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1.1.3.3">ℝ</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.2.m2.1c">\bar{\alpha}\colon\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> continuously
differentiable, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline"><semantics id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1a"><mi id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1.1" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1.1.cmml">σ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1b"><ci id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1.1">𝜎</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.3.m3.1c">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable and
