</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Numerical experiments and results</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After having introduced the optimal hedging problem
(<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) in Section <a href="#S3" title="3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and described in
Section <a href="#S4" title="4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> how one may numerically approximate the
solution by (<a href="#S4.Ex4" title="4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) using neural networks, we now turn
to numerical experiments to illustrate the feasibility of the
approach. We start by explaining in
Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1. Setting and Implementation ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> the modeling choices in
detail. The remainder of this section will then be devoted to
examining the following three questions:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2. Benchmark: No transaction costs ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>: How does neural network hedging
(for different risk-preferences) compare to the benchmark in a
Heston model without transaction costs?</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3. Price asymptotics under proportional transaction costs ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>: What is the effect of
proportional transaction costs on the exponential utility
indifference price?</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4. High-dimensional example ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>: Is the numerical method scalable to
higher dimensions?</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Setting and Implementation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.18" class="ltx_p">For the results presented here we have chosen a time horizon of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1a"><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml">30</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1.1">30</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.1.m1.1c">30</annotation></semantics></math>
trading days with daily rebalancing. Thus, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=30/365" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml">T</mi><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml">30</mn><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml">/</mo><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.3.cmml">365</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.1"></eq><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.2">𝑇</ci><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3"><divide id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.1"></divide><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.2">30</cn><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1.1.3.3">365</cn></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.2.m2.1c">T=30/365</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=30" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml">n</mi><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml">30</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.1"></eq><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.2">𝑛</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1.1.3">30</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.3.m3.1c">n=30</annotation></semantics></math> and the
trading dates are <math id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=i/365" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.2.cmml">t</mi><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.3.cmml">i</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.2.cmml">i</mi><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.1.cmml">/</mo><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.3.cmml">365</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.2">𝑡</ci><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.2.3">𝑖</ci></apply><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3"><divide id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.1"></divide><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.2">𝑖</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1.1.3.3">365</cn></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.4.m4.1c">t_{i}=i/365</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,\ldots,n" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3a"><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.2.cmml">i</mi><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.1.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.1.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.2.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.1.cmml">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal" id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.2.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.2.2.cmml">…</mi><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.2.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.1.cmml">,</mo><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.3.cmml">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4"><eq id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.1"></eq><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.2">𝑖</ci><list id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.4.3.2"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.1.1">0</cn><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.2.2">…</ci><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3.3">𝑛</ci></list></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.5.m5.3c">i=0,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. As explained in
Section <a href="#S4" title="4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Remark <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Remark 4.6. ‣ 4.2. Optimal hedging using deep neural networks ‣ 4. Approximating hedging strategies by deep neural networks ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>, the
number of units <math id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.2.cmml">δ</mi><msub id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.2.cmml">t</mi><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.3.cmml">i</mi></msub></msub><mo id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.1.cmml">∈</mo><msup id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.2.cmml">ℝ</mi><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.3.cmml">d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1"><in id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.1"></in><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.2">𝛿</ci><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.2">𝑡</ci><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.2.3.3">𝑖</ci></apply></apply><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.2">ℝ</ci><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1.1.3.3">𝑑</ci></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.6.m6.1c">\delta_{t_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that the agent decides to hold
in each of the instruments at <math id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1a"><msub id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.2.cmml">t</mi><mi id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.3.cmml">i</mi></msub><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1b"><apply id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.2">𝑡</ci><ci id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1.1.3">𝑖</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS1.p1.7.m7.1c">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is parametrized by a semi-recurrent
