pply><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.4.m2.3.3.2.2.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.4.m2.3.3.2.2.2.2.3">𝛾</ci></apply></apply></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.4.m2.3c">\mathrm{VaR}_{\gamma}(X):=\inf\{m\in\mathbb{R}\,:\mathbb{P}(X&lt;-m)\leq\gamma\}</annotation></semantics></math>. An alternative representation of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1a"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1.1.cmml">ρ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1b"><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1.1">𝜌</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.5.m3.1c">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> of type (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2. Optimized certainty equivalents ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>) is
discussed in Example <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Example 3.9. ‣ 3.2. Optimized certainty equivalents ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>. We refer to
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">FS16</a>, Section 4.4]</cite> for further details. Note that
different levels of <math id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1a"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1.1.cmml">α</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1b"><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1.1">𝛼</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.6.m4.1c">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to different levels of
risk-aversion, ranging from risk-neutral for <math id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1a"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1.1.cmml">α</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1b"><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1.1">𝛼</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.7.m5.1c">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> close to <math id="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1a"><mn id="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1.1.cmml">0</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.8.m6.1.1">0</cn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> to
very risk-averse for <math id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1a"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1.1.cmml">α</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1b"><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1.1">𝛼</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.9.m7.1c">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> close to <math id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1a"><mn id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1.1.cmml">1</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1.1">1</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.p1.10.m8.1c">1</annotation></semantics></math>. The limiting cases are
<math id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(X)=-\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2a"><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.cmml"><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.2.cmml">ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.3.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.3.2.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.cmml">(</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.1.1.cmml">X</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.3.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.1.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.cmml"><mo id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3a" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.cmml">−</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.2.cmml">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.1.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.2.1" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.1.1.cmml">[</mo><mi id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.2.cmml">X</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.3.2.3.1.1.cmml">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2b"><apply id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3"><eq id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2"><times id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.2.1"></times><ci id="S5.SS2.p1.11.m9.2.3.