<p id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">and consider <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{1},S^{2})" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2a"><mrow id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.3.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.3" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.3.cmml">(</mo><msup id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">S</mi><mn id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></msup><mo id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.4" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.3.cmml">,</mo><msup id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.2" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.2.cmml">S</mi><mn id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.3" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.3.cmml">2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.5" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.3.cmml">)</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2b"><interval closure="open" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2"><apply id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.2">𝑆</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.1.1.1.1.3">1</cn></apply><apply id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2">superscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.2">𝑆</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2.2.2.2.3">2</cn></apply></interval></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS2.SSSx1.p2.7.m1.2c">(S^{1},S^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> as the prices of liquidly tradeable assets.
A standard calculation<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>For example, one may use that <math id="footnote5.m1.3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\log(S^{1}),V)" display="inline"><semantics id="footnote5.m1.3b"><mrow id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.2" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.2.cmml">(</mo><mrow id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="footnote5.m1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m1.1.1.cmml">log</mi><mo id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1b" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml">⁡</mo><mrow id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml">(</mo><msup id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">S</mi><mn id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.3" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.3" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.2.cmml">,</mo><mi id="footnote5.m1.2.2" xref="footnote5.m1.2.2.cmml">V</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.4" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.2.cmml">)</mo></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="footnote5.m1.3c"><interval closure="open" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1"><apply id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1"><log id="footnote5.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.1.1"></log><apply id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1">superscript</csymbol><ci id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.2">𝑆</ci><cn type="integer" id="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.3.3.1.1.1.1.1.3">1</cn></apply></apply><ci id="footnote5.m1.2.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m1.2.2">𝑉</ci></interval></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="footnote5.m1.3d">(\log(S^{1}),V)</annotation></semantics></math>
is an affine process to see that the conditional expectation in (<a href="#S5.E3" title="In A brief reminder on the Heston model ‣ 5.2. Benchmark: No transaction costs ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>)
can be taken only with respect to <math id="footnote5.m2.4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(V_{t},s\in[0,t])" display="inline"><semantics id="footnote5.m2.4b"><mrow id="footnote5.m2.4.4" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.cmml"><mi id="footnote5.m2.4.4.3" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.3.cmml">σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.2.cmml">​</mo><mrow id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.cmml">(</mo><mrow id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.cmml"><mrow id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.2.cmml"><msub id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">V</mi><mi id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml">t</mi></msub><mo id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.2.cmml">,</mo><mi id="footnote5.m2.3.3" xref="footnote5.m2.3.3.cmml">s</mi></mrow><mo id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.2.cmml">∈</mo><mrow id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.1.cmml"><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.2.1" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">[</mo><mn id="footnote5.m2.1.1" xref="footnote5.m2.1.1.cmml">0</mn><mo id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.2.2" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">,</mo><mi id="footnote5.m2.2.2" xref="footnote5.m2.2.2.cmml">t</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.2.3" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.1.cmml">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.3" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.cmml">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="footnote5.m2.4c"><apply id="footnote5.m2.4.4.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4"><times id="footnote5.m2.4.4.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.2"></times><ci id="footnote5.m2.4.4.3.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.3">𝜎</ci><apply id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1"><in id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.2"></in><list id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1"><apply id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1">subscript</csymbol><ci id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.2">𝑉</ci><ci id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.1.1.1.3">𝑡</ci></apply><ci id="footnote5.m2.3.3.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.3.3">𝑠</ci></list><interval closure="closed" id="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.4.4.1.1.1.3.2"><cn type="integer" id="footnote5.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.1.1">0</cn><ci id="footnote5.m2.2.2.cmml" xref="footnote5.m2.2.2">𝑡</ci></interval></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="footnote5.m2.4d">\sigma(V_{t},s\in[0,t])</annotation></semantics></math>.
This conditional expectation can then be calculated by using the
SDE for <math id="footnote5.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline"><semantics id="footnote5.m3.1b"><mi id="footnote5.m3.1.1" xref="footnote5.m3.1.1.cmml">V</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="footnote5.m3.1c"><ci id="footnote5.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="footnote5.m3.1.1">𝑉</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="footnote5.m3.1d">V</annotation></semantics></math> or by directly inserting the expression from e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Duf01</a>, Section 3]</cite>.</span></span></span>
shows that (<a href="#S5.E3" title="In A brief reminder on the Heston model ‣ 5.2. Benchmark: No transaction costs ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) is given as</p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
