<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">and as <math id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">ε</mi><mo stretchy="false" id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml">↓</mo><mn id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">0</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1"><ci id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.1">↓</ci><ci id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.2">𝜀</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1.1.3">0</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS3.p3.1.m1.1c">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. One of the results in the
asymptotic analysis is that</p>
