continuous-time trading and no transaction costs, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1a"><mi id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1.1.cmml">Z</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1b"><ci id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1.1">𝑍</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p1.9.m9.1c">Z</annotation></semantics></math> can be
replicated perfectly by trading according to strategy
(<a href="#S5.E6" title="In A brief reminder on the Heston model ‣ 5.2. Benchmark: No transaction costs ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>) in each of the models. In particular, this
strategy is decoupled, i.e. the optimal holdings in
