<p id="S5.SS4.p2.13" class="ltx_p">By building <math id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1a"><mi id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1.1.cmml">δ</mi><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1b"><ci id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1.1">𝛿</ci></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p2.10.m1.1c">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> from the (discrete-time) variance optimal strategies for each of the <math id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1.1.cmml">5</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1.1">5</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p2.11.m2.1c">5</annotation></semantics></math> models, one sees from (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In 5.4. High-dimensional example ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>) that the minimal value of (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Remark 3.4. ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) over <span id="S5.SS4.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">all</span> <math id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.2.cmml">δ</mi><mo id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.1.cmml">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.3.cmml">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1"><in id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.1"></in><ci id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.2">𝛿</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1.1.3">ℋ</ci></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p2.12.m3.1c">\delta\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1.1.cmml">5</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1.1">5</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p2.13.m4.1c">5</annotation></semantics></math> times the minimal value of (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Remark 3.4. ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) associated to a single Heston model. This consideration serves as a guideline for assessing the approximation quality of the neural network strategy.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.13" class="ltx_p">To assess the scalability of the algorithm, we now calculate the
close-to-optimal neural network hedging strategy associated to
(<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Remark 3.4. ‣ 3. Pricing and hedging using convex risk measures ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) in both instances (i.e. for <math id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}=5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">5</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1.1.3">5</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.1.m1.1c">n_{H}=5</annotation></semantics></math> models and
for a single one, <math id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}=1" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1.1.3">1</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.2.m2.1c">n_{H}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) and compare the results. Unless
specified otherwise, the parameters are as in
Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1. Setting and Implementation ‣ 5. Numerical experiments and results ‣ Deep Hedging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>. Since for <math id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}=5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml">5</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1.1.3">5</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.3.m3.1c">n_{H}=5</annotation></semantics></math> we are
actually solving <math id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1.1.cmml">5</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1b"><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1.1">5</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.4.m4.1c">5</annotation></semantics></math> problems at once, we allow for a network with
more hidden nodes by taking <math id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}=N_{2}=12n_{H}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.2.cmml">N</mi><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.3.cmml">1</mn></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.3.cmml">=</mo><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.2.cmml">N</mi><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.3.cmml">2</mn></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.5" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.5.cmml">=</mo><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.2.cmml">12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.1.cmml">​</mo><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.3.cmml">H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1"><and id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1a.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1"></and><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1b.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.3"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.2">𝑁</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.2.3">1</cn></apply><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.2">𝑁</ci><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.3">2</cn></apply></apply><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1c.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.5.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.5"></eq><share href="#S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.4.cmml" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1d.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1"></share><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6"><times id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.1"></times><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.2">12</cn><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1.1.6.3.3">𝐻</ci></apply></apply></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.5.m5.1c">N_{1}=N_{2}=12n_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then train both
networks for a fixed number of time-steps (here <math id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{5}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml">2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.1.cmml">×</mo><msup id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.2.cmml">10</mn><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.3.cmml">5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1"><times id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.1"></times><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.2">2</cn><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3">superscript</csymbol><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.2">10</cn><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1.1.3.3">5</cn></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.6.m6.1c">2\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>) and
measure the performance in terms of both training time and realized
loss (evaluated on a test set of <math id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}\times 10^{5}" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.1.cmml">×</mo><msup id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.cmml"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.2.cmml">10</mn><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.3.cmml">5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1"><times id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.1"></times><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3">superscript</csymbol><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.2">10</cn><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1.1.3.3">5</cn></apply></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.7.m7.1c">n_{H}\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> sample paths): the
training times on a standard Lenovo X1 Carbon laptop are <math id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.75" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1.1.cmml">5.75</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1b"><cn type="float" id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1.1">5.75</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.8.m8.1c">5.75</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.1" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1.1.cmml">2.1</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1b"><cn type="float" id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1.1">2.1</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.9.m9.1c">2.1</annotation></semantics></math> hours for <math id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}=5" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.3.cmml">5</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1.1.3">5</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.10.m10.1c">n_{H}=5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{H}=1" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1a"><mrow id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.cmml"><msub id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.cmml"><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.2" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.2.cmml">n</mi><mi id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.3.cmml">H</mi></msub><mo id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.1.cmml">=</mo><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.3" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.3.cmml">1</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1b"><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1"><eq id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.1"></eq><apply id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2"><csymbol cd="ambiguous" id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2">subscript</csymbol><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.2.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.2">𝑛</ci><ci id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.2.3">𝐻</ci></apply><cn type="integer" id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.3.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1.1.3">1</cn></apply></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.11.m11.1c">n_{H}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively and the realized
losses are <math id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.13" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1.1.cmml">1.13</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1b"><cn type="float" id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1.1">1.13</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.12.m12.1c">1.13</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.20" display="inline"><semantics id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1a"><mn id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1.1" xref="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1.1.cmml">0.20</mn><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content" id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1b"><cn type="float" id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1.1.cmml" xref="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1.1">0.20</cn></annotation-xml><annotation encoding="application/x-tex" id="S5.SS4.p3.13.m13.1c">0.20</annotation></semantics></math>. In view of the considerations above,
this indicates that the approximation quality is roughly the same for
both instances (and close-to-optimal).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">While far from a systematic study, this last example nevertheless
demonstrates the potential of the algorithm for high-dimensional
hedging problems.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
